Block copies of GCC 4.0.4 as in the game's retail compiler (notes/COMPILER.md), for the
build psp-gcc-4.0.4a: the LBP-PSP-Decomp kit's psp-gcc-4.0.4c work tree plus this diff
(tools/gcc/build_404a.sh). Applies with `patch -p1` in gcc-4.0.4/ after the kit's diffs.
In config/mips/mips.c, mips_block_move_loop:
- a copy whose source or destination is not known to be word aligned tests the
  alignment at run time, as GCC 3.3's expand_block_move did (removed in GCC 3.4): one
  loop for the unaligned case, then one with lw/sw;
- the loop for an unaligned source or destination stores two words, advances both
  pointers, then stores the last two at -8/-4 (word-aligned copies keep the kit's
  order, change C1).
GCC code is GPL-2.0-or-later (GCC 4.0.4) and the kit's context GPL-3.0-or-later.
